    "modified_layer_sha256": "0117849fb0e52b0840a35a1f5249d468d76ce08474b743be396de910a436ab8e",
    "method": "Manual old-vkroots-API backport of event-queue isolation, proxy ownership and teardown fixes; registry startup uses one private roundtrip rather than an initial blocking dispatch."
  },
  "validation": {
    "compile": "The complete private builder downloaded and verified the nine pinned inputs, applied and verified the patch, compiled and linked on Linux x86-64, and resolved dependencies before publication. This establishes buildability, not game compatibility.",
    "runtime": "HDR transport was demonstrated in one GTA V Enhanced Story Mode session on Intel OXP3/CachyOS with XeSS SR, RenoDX and frame generation disabled. HDR10/PQ/BT.2020/R10 output and compositor HDR-input feedback were verified; the owner reported HDR, gameplay and HUD looked correct in that run. Subsequent cold starts froze or exited even with frame generation disabled and the previously used settings restored.",
    "limits": "The queue patch is not an established startup fix. One successful Story Mode HDR session does not establish reliable game compatibility; later cold-start failures remain unresolved. No guarantee for frame generation, other applications, long play, suspend/resume or future versions. Captured thread locations did not establish a WSI/Wayland/XCB blocking frame, so an event-queue deadlock is unproven.",
    "status": "experimental candidate; HDR transport demonstrated once, reliable cold startup unresolved"
  },
